{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/442","id":4819345479,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-508s8AAAABH0FgRw","html_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/442","diff_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/442.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/442.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/442","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/442/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/442/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/442/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/statuses/4e16d001d505d4f21dd2bcfc44591f9be4c279bd","number":442,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Conditional κ ≈ 1.2375517e-3: idle-axis hosting of helper residuals (+9.2% over #434)","user":{"login":"DaysSky","id":88261516,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MjYxNTE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88261516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky","html_url":"https://github.com/DaysSky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Conditional **κ = 618775866623647/(5·10¹⁷) ≈ 1.237551733247294·10⁻³**, **+9.218% over #434** (1.133100552284434·10⁻³). The bit supplier binds. It is also +8.67% above the newest posted value, #441 (1.138798055343319·10⁻³). Hosting changes only the global template, so it should stack on #440/#441's R740 word as well.\n\n## Change and mathematical scope\n\nIn the compressed nine-stage window, idle data pairs are brought to the active level by idle advance children (ranks 48/32/16/8 for complex, 42/28/14/7 for bit). These children are about a sixth of the paid cost.\n\nA dirty helper residual acts on whatever stream owns it as an exact coordinate factor, independent of the stream's contents. That is the inherited correlated dirty-bank fact that banks already rely on. It is the same kind of factor an idle child applies to its pending coordinates. So a helper residual can be owned by an idle data family instead of a bank slot, on coordinates that family would advance later, and the child keeps only the rest.\n\nThe validity condition is a window: the family must be untouched (no local invocation on its pair, no bridge naming it) between the hosting invocation and its advance. Neither local word changes.\n\n## Result\n\n| supplier | parent saving | hosted saving | live stock | max child | hosted residuals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| bit, m = 64, #434 R747 | 1.134386·10⁻³ | **1.239085·10⁻³** | 14,259 → 9,457 | 42 → 8 | 39,568 of 53,784 |\n| complex, m = 73, #433 R560 | 1.183987·10⁻³ | **1.267453·10⁻³** | 12,720 → 8,400 | 48 → 8 | 34,560 of 40,320 |\n\nThe rank deficit stays at 2496 on both sides.\n\n## Validation\n\n`python -B research/idle-axis-hosting/verify.py /absolute/new/output` uses the standard library only. It:\n\n1. runs #434's complete verifier from scratch;\n2. regenerates both hosted templates from #434's fresh outputs and a frozen integer-programme selection (`--discover` recomputes the selection with scipy);\n3. runs an independent audit that shares no code with the generators:\n   - windows re-derived from each schedule;\n   - for every invocation and replica: exactly one owner per helper, and slots in window, inside their child's pending set, disjoint, and off the active pair;\n   - exact remainder children, exact bank tiling, a recomputed profile and deficit;\n   - nine mutation controls rejected;\n4. computes two rational moments per supplier and fresh finite invoices with the hosted stock:\n   - two extra route factors are charged per helper selector;\n   - the parent's larger complex per-vertex bill is kept;\n5. runs #434's strict outer assembly: six bootstrap levels and all 47 inequalities, with the next grid point and the zero-η, zero-β and unit-β controls rejected.\n\n### Open obligations\n\n[PROOF.md](research/idle-axis-hosting/PROOF.md) gives the hosting lemma. It extends the inherited correlated dirty-bank / compressed-window interface to data streams during idle windows; that extension is the principal review point. The global operator identity is argued, not replayed numerically on the address spaces, as for the parents' banks.\n\nThe all-size compiler, restored-work, tape/common-grid, precision and analytic interfaces remain inherited assumptions. No Lean proof and no unconditional integer-multiplication theorem is claimed.\n\n## Credits and AI disclosure\n\nThis builds on and runs unchanged:\n\n- #434 (Rohan Arun, OpenAI Codex);\n- #433 (icekylinx);\n- #435/#417 (chafreaky);\n- #426 (ai-nanachi);\n- #425/#386 (Zhihao Chen, OpenAI Codex);\n- #370 (Dylan Crow);\n- Jacob Sussman's E8 unit and interfaces.\n\nThe hosting construction, generators, audit and assembly were prepared with assistance from Claude. No inherited file is changed.\n\nLocal transcript: `PASS_FULL_IDLE_AXIS_HOSTING_COMPOSITION` on macOS (Apple silicon) with Python 3.14.8 and Python 3.12.13; each run replays #434 in full (about 2 minutes) before the hosting steps. CI covers Python 3.11 and 3.14.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-11T13:18:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T13:18:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0c1f1891c47b20efcf973dfeaf9e944e55de180f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"DaysSky:research/idle-axis-hosting","ref":"research/idle-axis-hosting","repo":{"id":1411331924,"node_id":"R_kgDOVB83VA","name":"integer-mult-bounds","full_name":"DaysSky/integer-mult-bounds","owner":{"login":"DaysSky","id":88261516,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MjYxNTE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88261516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky","html_url":"https://github.com/DaysSky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaysSky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Conditional integer multiplication: kappa > 2^-15. Community proofs, exact certificates and reproducible audits; assumes the OpenAI #109 framework.","homepage":null,"language":null,"visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":0,"open_issues":0,"size":92754,"default_branch":"main","has_issues":false,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_downloads":f